# --- Access codes (client) ---
# Three independent codes. Each one is optional: when a variable is left empty,
# the development fallback shown below applies IN PRODUCTION TOO — set all three
# for a real deployment, not just the admin one.
#
# Admin: manage the roster, schedule matches, call up players, plan trainings,
# enter championship results, correct stats after the game. Fallback: "admin".
VITE_ADMIN_PASSWORD=admin
# Scorer's table: start a match, score, fouls, substitutions, clock, and
# "finish the match" — which freezes the score for good. Fallback: "marque".
VITE_SCORER_PASSWORD=marque
# Player: grants NO write access at all. It only unlocks picking your own name
# in the roster, so the app can show you your stats. Fallback: "joueur".
VITE_PLAYER_PASSWORD=joueur
#
# These codes are compiled into the bundle and readable in the browser's dev
# tools. They guard against accidents between people who trust each other, not
# against a malicious third party. The door the server actually guards is
# WRITE_TOKEN, below.

# --- Server: the database. REQUIRED. ---
# The single source of truth: every read and every write goes to it, and the
# application has nothing to show without it. Vercel's Neon integration fills
# DATABASE_URL in for you; use the POOLED connection string (its host ends in
# `-pooler`), because a serverless function holds no connection between
# invocations.
# Locally: `docker compose up -d` then
#   psql "postgres://swish:swish@localhost:5433/swish" -f db/schema.sql
DATABASE_URL=

# Guards every **write**. Reading is public — the schedule, the standings and the
# team message are not confidential, and provisioning a secret onto every phone
# that only ever reads costs more than it buys.
# NOT prefixed VITE_ — unlike the three codes above, this one must never reach
# the bundle: it is checked by the server, not by the client. Any long random
# string. Each device that writes enters it once, under Administration → Write
# access.
# The API refuses to write while this is empty. That is deliberate: a database
# with no token would be open to anyone who knows the URL.
WRITE_TOKEN=
